  "result": "Fixed. Option names in `--help` now list the short form first, so `-v, --verbose` renders instead of `--verbose, -v`.\n\n**Cause:** `join_options` in `src/click/formatting.py` sorted the option names by prefix length with `reverse=True`, which put the longer `--` form first. I removed the `reverse=True`. Names with the same prefix length keep their declaration order.\n\n**Test:** I added `test_option_names_sorted_short_before_long` to `tests/test_formatting.py`. It fails without the fix and passes with it.\n\n**Results:** The full suite passes (1907 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed). Nothing is committed.\n\nI didn't add a `CHANGES.md` entry. The project keeps one with issue and PR references, so you may want to add one.",
